    "prompt": "ATTACH THE APPROVED PAGE 4 AND PAGE 3 RENDERS - the button put down on page 3 comes back here.\nCAMERA: medium close-up, eye level on the boards. TinyMouse in the open doorway LEFT, PuppyCub\n  lying with its chin on the floor RIGHT - 🔴 both at THE SAME DEPTH, clear space between.\nSUBJECT: TinyMouse stands on the threshold on two legs, one hand raised in greeting, the other\n  still on the door, half its body out; ears up, whiskers forward, eyes bright; its apron carries\n  thread-ends and sawdust. PuppyCub lies flat with its chin on the boards to bring its eyes level,\n  forepaws together, eyes wide, mouth open, tail sweeping.\nLIGHT: MORNING - the tinted bundle lies between them with the jam bowl in it, and a warmer light\n  #E0A85A comes out of the doorway. 🔴 Nothing inside it is cut but that glow.\nDOOR: 🔴 THE SIZE CHAIN CLOSES. The mouse is shorter than the door, the door is one puppy forepaw\n  tall, so the mouse is smaller than the puppy's nose - all three at one depth. Use the scale plate.\nRED: 🔴 THE RECOVERY - the button given away on page 3 is fitted to the outer face of the door as\n  its handle, just right for two small hands. Same four holes, same red, the one red here.\nFINISH: 2 (the mouse + the puppy's face). 0 lettering."
